================================================================================
STEP 9 - A private local repository, so the build never writes the shared one
================================================================================
The clone instantiation instructions place /root/.m2/repository in the shared,
read-only, safe-for-concurrent-use set, alongside /opt/spark-src and the rulesets: a
sibling is probably mid-scan against them. A full reactor resolves dependencies the
provisioned NARROWED build never needed - there is no org/apache/kafka in the primed
repository at all - so building against the shared path would WRITE into it. The
primed repository is therefore copied once into this clone's own scratch and the build
is pointed at the copy with -Dmaven.repo.local. The shared original is read, and is
modified by neither the copy nor the build - the one unrelated write into it during
this session is disclosed at STEP 8; the counts below are taken before the copy and
again after the build, and
the difference is the independent record of what this build resolved.

