CROSS-REFERENCES - ONE MEASUREMENT, CITED MORE THAN ONCE
================================================================================

AAP 0.6.4: a figure appearing in two documents must be one measurement cited twice,
never two measurements. This file is the measurement for the build. What it cites
from elsewhere, and what must be cited from it, in both directions:

  WHAT THIS FILE CITES RATHER THAN RE-MEASURES

  harness/artifacts/logs/maven-preflight.log
    owns the Maven verdict. STEP 8 quotes it verbatim - detected 3.9.11, required
    3.9.11, normalized 003009011 on both sides, the '[ -ne ]' predicate exiting 1,
    DOWNLOAD_BRANCH_TAKEN=no, verdict PASS - and runs no version comparison of its
    own. The underlying facts are host-global and shared read-only: the same
    /usr/local/bin/mvn and the same <maven.version>3.9.11</maven.version>, which
    STEP 5 reads again only because the tree it reads is a different tree. What
    STEP 8 does measure, because it is genuinely new, is the build tree's own
    build/ directory: no apache-maven* distribution, so install_mvn()'s early
    return is not taken and its download conditional is reached and evaluates
    false. The wrapper's own 'Using `mvn` from path: /usr/local/bin/mvn' in PART 2
    is the confirmation after the fact, and STEP 15 shows build/ unchanged.

  harness/artifacts/logs/gate-record.json
    recorded the same Maven identity at the gate, and the JDK figure STEP 7
    re-measures under the sourced environment. Both agree with this file.

  harness/ENVIRONMENT.md
    is the provisioning record, and is cited for what the provisioning did, never
    for what this build did. Two of its figures are load-bearing here and both are
    quoted as its own: the NARROWED build command in section 5 with its 33-project
    reactor and 32 of 32 JAR projects, and the 32 named JAR producers in section 6
    from which the six-module difference above is derived by set difference. Its
