  WHAT MUST BE CITED FROM THIS FILE

  oss-scan-results/build-record.md
    the Maven pre-check verdict beside the build command; the exact command with
    its five flags and the flag-to-module arithmetic; the 40 / 38 / 2 reactor
    arithmetic; the per-project outcome for all 40 projects, taken from PART 2's
    reactor summary together with STEP 13's on-disk confirmation; the two
    pom-packaging projects marked expected; the six unlisted JAR producers as a
    recorded difference; and the statement that no diagnostic pass was needed.
    It must not re-derive any of them by running anything again.

  harness/artifacts/logs/cpg-input-inventory.json
    STEP 13's per-project artifact paths, and in particular the two that are not in
    their build directory's root: examples' main artifact under
    target/scala-2.13/jars, and common/network-yarn's unattached shaded shuffle jar
    under target/scala-2.13. TWO CAUTIONS, so this file and the inventory cannot be
    read as disagreeing. First, every path in STEP 13 is relative to the build tree
    named under SUBJECT, not to SPARK_SRC. Second, every sha256 in STEP 13 is of
    THIS build's artifacts: a jar entry carries a build timestamp, so a second build
    of identical source produces a different digest, and the cross-check between
    the two documents is project -> outcome and artifact -> relative path, never a
    digest comparison. A digest difference between two builds is not a discrepancy;
    a missing project or a differently located artifact would be.

  oss-scan-results/run-record.md
    indexes this file as the evidence behind the build. The figures to cite are the
    exit code 0, BUILD SUCCESS, the 40-project reactor with 38 JAR-packaging
