  - It did not write to /opt/spark-src. That tree is shared read-only with
    concurrent clones which may be mid-scan against it and its build output. STEP 3
    recorded its state before the build and STEP 15 re-read it after: same HEAD,
    zero modified tracked entries, the same 31 build directories, and the same
    seven still absent.
  - The build wrote to no shared path: not the shared /root/.m2/repository, not the
    rulesets, not the feed caches, not the graph. It resolved against the private
    copy, and STEP 15 re-reads the shared repository to find the same 867 jars and
    5,832 files as STEP 9, and still no org/apache/kafka. The one write into that
    shared repository during this session was not the build's, and STEP 8 discloses
    it in full: three model-building poms fetched by a stray bare 'mvn' at
    18:51:25Z, before the STEP 9 baseline and before the build began.
  - It did not narrow the reactor, drop a flag, exclude a module, or retry anything
    with reduced scope to make it pass. There is no -pl and no -am in the
    invocation, and STEP 10 shows both absent in the script that ran it.
  - It did not install, upgrade or substitute anything. The wrapper's Maven
    download branch was ruled out before the build by the pre-check, not observed
    not to have fired, and STEP 8 and STEP 15 show build/ holding only its six
    checked-in scripts.
  - It did not run any Spark test suite, in any language. The build carries
    -DskipTests and no test goal appears in the invocation. Test-classified
    artifacts that the packaging phase produced are recorded at STEP 13 as
    artifacts; nothing in them was executed.
  - It did not modify any Apache Spark file, in either tree. Both trees end with
    zero modified tracked entries.
  - It did not classify artifacts into a graph input set, or exclude any artifact
    from one. STEP 13 separates a project's own output from copied dependencies
    only so that 'this project produced its own artifact' can be asserted at all;
    the input set is cpg-input-inventory.json's to build.
  - It did not judge, rank, compare or interpret anything any scanner reported. No
    finding of any kind appears in this file.
  - It did not tear anything down. The build tree, its output and the private local
    repository are left exactly where they are (AAP 0.8.1).
  - It did not use GITHUB_TOKEN or any other credential: the fetch at STEP 4 is
